we spent several hours testing and  breaking down aftermarket ps4  controllers here at GameSpot in hopes of  finding the best one and we got our  hands on four of them the Razer eyes you  make on revolution scuff infinity for PS  Pro and scuff impact so which one is the  best the answer really depends on two  factors the features you want and how  much you're willing to spend let's start  with some basics do you absolutely need  your controller to be Wireless if so you  probably won't want the rise you our  revolution since both only work when  they're wired they're designed with  competitive play in mind so it's  understandable why despite being the  bulkiest the riser is the most  comfortable to hold the scuff infinity  for PS pro is identical to the DualShock  4 while the impact closely resembles the  xbox controller and both come with  rubbery grips on the handles the  revolution has a nice chalky grip but  the trigger shape and the trigger  placement hamper its ergonomics with  that said the revolution had the least  desirable triggers and unfortunately it  can be a deal-breaker  they're far too stiff and take on an  awkward shape that messes with natural  hand positioning the riser stands above  the rest  since l2 and r2 are effortless to pull  and there are optional trigger stops to  shorten the throw scuffs controllers  look and feel similar to the DualShock 4  though you can lighten the resistance  adjust the trigger stops and swap in  extended trigger caps and what's a  premium controller without extra buttons  or paddles all four controllers offer  programmable buttons on the back end to  help keep your thumbs on the sticks at  all times the revolution is the best if  you only need two extra buttons the  outer buttons are placed perfectly while  the innermost ones are kind of hard to  use the riser works wonderfully as well  with the two triggers on the back and  two extra bumpers on top which all feel  tactile similar to mouse clicks scuffs  paddles weren't bad at all but they felt  the least natural to use scuff and razor  allow you to program these buttons on  the fly while Nikon requires you to  connect to a PC and using software to  tweak the controllers functions but it's  worth noting that nay con lets you tweak  the finest details of your controller  input the only controller that really  improves upon the face buttons is the  rise you there's soft and tactile also  identical to clicking a mouse it takes a  little getting  - but it makes for the most responsive  buttons all 4 controllers have analog  sticks that felt better than the  DualShock 4 since they offered better  grip and fluid movement for precise  aiming the revolutions and Raichu sticks  are lighter to the touch and have a  consistent resistance if we want to get  picky we'd say that these have a slight  edge though we can't write off what  scuff offers especially since these have  the best grip if there's one thing that  could kill your interest in these  controllers it's their price each one  cost well over 100 US dollars and the  ratio and revolution are only available  in Sony EMEA markets us buyers will have  to consider the nebulous cost of  importing scuffs infinity for PS pro  starts at $130 and the impact at $140  and any add-ons will cost a bit more  what if the best ps4 controller was in  front of us all along if we're  accounting for price I'd say the  DualShock 4 is pretty cost effective it  doesn't do anything special but also  doesn't do anything wrong but if you're  willing to shell out the dough and  itching for something more I would  recommend the razor rise you it's a bit  disappointing that while each controller  has some amazing features and  improvements over the DualShock 4 none  of them nailed down everything we want  however one gripe we may have with one  controller may not affect you in the  slightest  what chances are you'll have to make  some compromises either way after all  it's up to you to decide what matters  most in your purchase if you want a more  detailed breakdown of each controller  check out our reviews on them I hope you  found this video helpful so give us a  thumbs up and if you want more videos  like this be sure to subscribe to  GameSpot thanks for watching  you
 

